# Airflow's .airflowignore uses regular expressions by default
# (AIRFLOW__CORE__DAG_IGNORE_FILE_SYNTAX=regexp).
#
# common.py is a shared library, not a DAG file. It imports `airflow`, so the DagBag's
# safe-mode heuristic would otherwise open and parse it on every scheduler loop only to
# find no DAG in it. Ignoring it here skips that work; it stays importable, because
# .airflowignore governs DAG *discovery*, not sys.path.
^common\.py$
